{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>A mamzer shall not enter the assembly of YHWH.</b> He is not permitted to take a daughter of Israel, but he is permitted in a female convert, for the Torah said 'the assembly of YHWH,' and the assembly of converts is not called 'the assembly of YHWH.' And the meaning of mamzer is one born of those forbidden relations that carry karet or the death penalty of the court. And in the Yerushalmi of Kiddushin, Rabbi Abbahu said: What is a mamzer? A strange blemish (mum zar)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:28.745347669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}